From 805d458823296215047bd286110a14b7856cb49a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pooya Parsa <pooya@pi0.io>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 21:12:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/virtio: wait up to 30 s for a capset, and killably

A host may make its 3D renderer only when the guest first asks for a
capset: unkernel loads virglrenderer, compiled to WebAssembly, and a
WebGL2 context on the guest's first GL use, which fetches about 185 KB
over the network. Five seconds is short for that on a slow link, and on a
timeout DRM_IOCTL_VIRTGPU_GET_CAPS gives -EBUSY, which Mesa takes for no
caps, so the client falls back to software rendering although the answer
comes moments later and serves every later client from the cache.

Wait up to 30 s, and let a fatal signal end the wait, since a task now
waits long enough for someone to want to kill it.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_ioctl.c | 12 ++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_ioctl.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_ioctl.c
index 81e70a12b35..53f563fd734 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_ioctl.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_ioctl.c
@@ -468,8 +468,16 @@ static int virtio_gpu_get_caps_ioctl(struct drm_device *dev,
 	virtio_gpu_notify(vgdev);
 
 copy_exit:
-	ret = wait_event_timeout(vgdev->resp_wq,
-				 atomic_read(&cache_ent->is_valid), 5 * HZ);
+	/*
+	 * A host may start its 3D renderer only when a capset is first asked
+	 * for (it may have to fetch it), so give it longer than the replies to
+	 * other commands, but let a fatal signal end the wait.
+	 */
+	ret = wait_event_killable_timeout(vgdev->resp_wq,
+					  atomic_read(&cache_ent->is_valid),
+					  30 * HZ);
+	if (ret < 0)
+		return ret;
 	if (!ret)
 		return -EBUSY;
 
-- 
2.56.0

